---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import { ogPathFor } from '../data/og'

// Draft for Ari's review. Facts come from the public Desk, factory and
// Ouro MD repositories; re-check them before publishing.
const title = 'Privacy | Ouroboros'
const description = 'What this site, hosted Desk, the factory and Ouro MD collect, in plain language.'
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogPathFor('/privacy')} canonical="https://ouroboros.bot/privacy/">
  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-24 pt-32 pb-8 md:pt-44">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <span class="eyebrow block mb-6">Privacy</span>
      <h1 class="heading-lead">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 inline-flex tag tag-alpha">Draft for review</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-24 pb-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose-ouro">
      <p>This page says what this site and each of our tools collect, in plain language. If something here is wrong or unclear, ask your agent to file an issue on the project it's about.</p>

      <h2>This site</h2>
      <p>You don't need an account to read it. It sets no cookies and loads no analytics script of its own. Cloudflare serves the pages and, like any web host, sees each request.</p>

      <h2>Hosted Desk</h2>
      <p>Hosted Desk is not open yet. When it is, you sign in with GitHub so it can confirm who you are, and only accounts on its allow list get in. It keeps a copy of your desk's Git repository on our server so it can read and write your tasks and notes, and pushes its changes back to your repository. It can't run commands or change code. We'll publish a full notice for it before it opens to anyone else.</p>

      <h2>The factory</h2>
      <p>Desk asks you once whether you want to contribute to <a href="https://ourostack.github.io/factory/">the factory</a>. Contributing is off unless you say yes. Desk keeps its own session notes on your machine either way; only publishing waits for your yes.</p>
      <p>If you say yes, Desk publishes measurements of how your agent sessions ran to the public <a href="https://github.com/ourostack/factory">ourostack/factory</a> repository: how long they took, how time split between turns, tools and waits, which tools failed or retried, which models and plugin versions ran, which public pull requests a session touched, the day a job finished, whether you accepted the result, and the rough size (not the text) of each prompt and reply. It never includes transcript text, prompts, file contents, names or the time of day. Each contribution arrives as a pull request, so your GitHub account and when you contributed are visible on GitHub.</p>

      <h2>Ouro MD</h2>
      <p>Builds from the installer or the download page send anonymous usage telemetry to PostHog, on by default: app launches, update steps, and when documents are opened, saved, renamed or exported, with the app and macOS version and a random install id. It never sends document contents, filenames, folder paths, search queries or clipboard contents. Turn it off in Settings &rsaquo; Telemetry. The app checks GitHub for updates. The full list is in <a href="https://github.com/ourostack/ouro-md/blob/main/PRIVACY.md">Ouro MD's PRIVACY.md</a>.</p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Each project takes issues on <a href="https://github.com/ourostack">GitHub</a>. Ask your agent to file one on the project your question is about.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
